>	1)  how can you open up boxes with the key?
>	    had hexagonal key for a hexagonal lock but
>	    now what the hell do I do?
>
(a)pply the key in the direction of the box (a "." if you're standing on the
box).  Beware, a hexagonal key will not necessarily open a hexagonal lock...
at least on my version.  Odd.  If you id it as a skeleton key, it will open
any box, chest, door, etc.

>	2)  why won't the shopkeeper let you 
>	    out of the shop once you're in?
>
You're probably carrying something from the shop that you haven't paid for.
"P" pays the debt (okay, exact key depends on version and customization).  Or,
perhaps you zapped a wand or ate some food he owned, and he wants paid.

>	3)  what good are statues? 
>
Not much.  If you (a)pply a pickaxe at them, the rubble will occasionally
contain a spellbook (very rare).  If you see a bunch on the same level, watch
out for Medusa (better yet, don't watch...)!

>	4) will your pet follow you down to other levels?
>	   a few times I came back up and the kitten/dog
>	   turned nasty on me.  Do you need a leash? 
>	
Yes, but they must be adjacent to you when you use the stairs.  Whistles
(especially magic ones) can help you get them to tag along.  If you abandon
your pet, he'll eventually go wild (tame them by throwing food...tripe is
best).  Leashes can be useful, but pets tend to break out of them rather
quickly.

